      "text": "Automatic Theorem Proving in Walnut — 42 sections: Front matter; Introduction; Basics\n\n**Automatic Theorem Proving in Walnut**\n\n*Hamoon Mousavi*\n\n34 pp, 42 sections.\n\n**Outline.** Front matter; 1 Introduction; 2 Basics; 2.1 Words and Automata; 2.2 Number Systems; 2.3 Automatic Words; 2.4 Automata accepting Predicates; 3 Syntax and Semantic of Predicates in Walnut; 3.1 Alphabets; 3.2 Arithmetic and Alphabetic Constants; 3.3 Variables; 3.4 Operators; 3.5 Arithmetic Expressions; 3.6 Indexing Expressions and Their Semantic Ru; 3.7 Calling Expressions and Their Semantic Rul; 3.8 Relative Expressions; 3.9 Predicates; 4 Decision Procedure: Walnut's Implementation",
